    "summary": "Acoustic gems, tight jams, stellar The Other One → Lovelight",
    "blurb": "The set shines with a crisp acoustic segment featuring Friend Of The Devil and Candyman, then builds into high‑energy rock with Good Lovin', The Other One into Turn On Your Lovelight. Jerry’s vocals are sweet and his guitar locks in with Phil’s solid bass throughout.",
    "review": "April 3, 1970 at the Field House captures a Grateful Dead that balances delicate acoustic storytelling with powerhouse electric jamming. Early on the band rolls out an intimate acoustic set—Jerry’s lyric‑focused take on Friend Of The Devil and a debuting Candyman showcase his surprisingly sweet vocal tone, while Pigpen’s presence is felt in the soulful Good Lovin' homage. The second half ramps up the excitement: China Cat Sunflower segues into I Know You Rider with classic chemistry, then a relentless drive carries through Good Lovin', a tight drum groove, and culminates in an explosive The Other One → Turn On Your Lovelight that leaves the audience buzzing. Highlights like Wake Up Little Susie (acoustic) and the seamless transition from NFA into Lovelight add extra sparkle to an already memorable night.",
